        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "fix: keep plugin update output tails utf8-safe",
        "body": "AI-assisted: yes\n\n## What Problem This Solves\n\nFixes an issue where plugin update proof diagnostics could show replacement characters when a bounded output tail started in the middle of a multibyte UTF-8 character. That made failure evidence noisier and less trustworthy when plugin update logs included non-ASCII output near the retained tail boundary.\n\n## Why This Change Was Made\n\nThe probe now decodes the retained byte suffix from the first valid UTF-8 boundary before printing the diagnostic tail. The byte cap remains unchanged, so the proof output stays bounded while avoiding malformed text at the beginning of the tail.\n\nRelated independent bug-family PRs: this is one UTF-8-safe bounded-output fix. It is independent of the cross-OS release-check tail fix and does not depend on any other branch.\n\n## User Impact\n\nDevelopers and maintainers get readable plugin update diagnostics for non-ASCII logs without losing the existing output-size bound.\n\n## Evidence\n\nCurrent head: `0c966fae23b1e41439cdd4898caa3d61abfe0b5f`\n\n- `node scripts/run-vitest.mjs test/scripts/plugin-update-unchanged-docker.test.ts -t \"UTF-8\"` passed after rebasing onto current `upstream/main`.\n- `git diff --check upstream/main..HEAD` passed.",
